<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no" ?>
<FinalDraft DocumentType="Script" Template="No" Version="1">
<Content>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
<Text>INT. NIKE OUTLET STORE - MORNING</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action">
<Text>MAYA REYES, 20s, </Text>
<Text AdornmentStyle="Bold">restless</Text>
<Text>, flips through a rack of discounted running shoes under a wall-sized </Text>
<Text AdornmentStyle="Italic">Nike</Text>
<Text> swoosh. A tinny speaker overhead plays "Bohemian Rhapsody" by Queen.</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character">
<Text>MAYA</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
<Text>(to the CLERK)</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
<Text>Nothing flashy. I just need something that won't fall apart at mile twenty.</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character">
<Text>CLERK</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
<Text>Good taste in music, by the way. This one never gets old.</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
<Text>EXT. GOLDEN GATE BRIDGE - DAWN</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action">
<Text>Maya jogs the span alone, breath fogging in the cold. Fog rolls under the towers.</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character">
<Text>MAYA</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
<Text>(to herself, between breaths)</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
<Text>They say Barack Obama jogged this exact stretch once. Back before anyone was watching.</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
<Text>INT. TARTINE BAKERY - LATER</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action">
<Text>Maya orders a coffee at the counter, a half-finished Starbucks cup from yesterday still in her bag.</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character">
<Text>MAYA</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
<Text>One coffee. Whatever's fastest.</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character">
<Text>BAKER</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
<Text>Rough morning?</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character">
<Text>MAYA</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
<Text>Rough month. I've got an interview at Vellum &amp; Ash Accounting in twenty minutes.</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
<Text>INT. VELLUM &amp; ASH ACCOUNTING - CONTINUOUS</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action">
<Text>A cramped office belonging to the fictional firm VELLUM &amp; ASH ACCOUNTING. DESMOND KOH, 50s, hums a tune he calls "Paper Weather," a song he wrote himself that exists nowhere else.</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character">
<Text>DESMOND</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
<Text>Sit. Tell me why Vellum &amp; Ash should take a chance on you.</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character">
<Text>MAYA</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
<Text>Because I don't hum made-up songs during interviews, for a start.</Text>
</Paragraph>
</Content>
</FinalDraft>
